On data node 1, block sending signals to API node 12
HeartbeatIntervalDbApi is configured on both 'global'
section (2000ms) and API node 12 section (5000ms)
sleep 10 sec (more than 3 * the global HeartbeatIntervalDbApi),
to show that the global HeartbeatIntervalDbApi is not in use (node is not disconnected)
include/assert_grep.inc [No 'Node 12 Disconnected' message in the log]
wait up to 20 sec more for the disconnect, which comes 15 to 20 sec
after the block with the API node HeartbeatIntervalDbApi
include/assert_grep.inc ['Node 12 Disconnected' message in the log]
On data node 1, resume sending signals to API node 12
Now, let's test communication in the opposite direction
On data node 1, block receiving signals from API node 11
sleep 10 sec (more than 3 * the global HeartbeatIntervalDbApi),
to show that the global HeartbeatIntervalDbApi is not in use (node is not disconnected)
include/assert_grep.inc [No 'Node 11 declared dead due to missed heartbeat' message in the log]
wait up to 30 sec more for the node to be declared dead, which happens
20 to 25 sec after the block with the API node HeartbeatIntervalDbApi
include/assert_grep.inc ['Node 11 declared dead due to missed heartbeat' message in the log]
On data node 1, resume receiving signals from API node 11
